cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use UAV-EW-Bench-2026, please cite it as below."
title: "UAV-EW-Bench-2026: A Reproducible Benchmark for Adversarially-Robust UAV Navigation under Electronic-Warfare Jamming"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Anaedevha"
    given-names: "Roger Nick"
    affiliation: "National Research Nuclear University MEPhI"
keywords:
  - UAV
  - electronic warfare
  - GNSS spoofing
  - adversarial robustness
  - mission completion
  - jamming-to-signal ratio
  - DO-326A
abstract: >
  UAV-EW-Bench-2026 measures autonomous-UAV mission-completion as a
  function of electronic-warfare jamming intensity (jamming-to-signal
  ratio, dB) under a combined adversarial contour (GNSS spoofing, PGD
  visual perturbation, BIM DRL-policy attack), across three mission
  profiles and three simulated GNSS receiver models, for four defence
  configurations. Completion is labelled per DO-326A/ED-202A. Ships with
  a reproducible generation harness (analytical Monte-Carlo backend and a
  full-fidelity AirSim/PX4 SITL backend).
